t="epo"><addressbook><name>OHKAWA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADOKORO TOYOYASU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKAI HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIPPON SEIKI CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHKAWA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADOKORO, TOYOYASU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKAI, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHKAWA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADOKORO TOYOYASU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKAI HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHKAWA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADOKORO, TOYOYASU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKAI, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An electroluminescent display comprises a transparent substrate (1) on which are formed a transparent electrode (2), an auxiliary electrode (3) having a resistivity smaller than that of the transparent electrode (2), an intermediate insulating layer (4) formed on the transparent electrode (2) except on the display electrode (21) and the terminal (22), a luminescent layer (5) formed on the display electrode (21) and the insulating layer (4), and a back electrode (6) arranged on the luminescent layer (5) and opposed to the display electrode (21). The transparent electrode (2) is separated into functionally different portions including display electrodes (21) formed of a plurality of pixel segments of specific shape, terminals (22) led toward the peripheries of the transparent substrate (1), and wiring electrodes (23) for connecting between the terminals (22) and the display electrodes (21). The transparent electrode further includes terminals (24) for back electrodes (6).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un écran électroluminescent comprenant un substrat transparent (1) sur lequel sont formées une électrode transparente (2), une électrode auxiliaire (3) présentant une résistivité inférieure à celle de l'électrode transparente (2), une couche isolante intermédiaire (4) formée sur l'électrode transparente (2) ne recouvrant ni l'électrode d'affichage (21) ni la borne (22), une couche luminescente (5) reposant sur l'électrode d'affichage (21) et la couche isolante (4) et une électrode arrière (6) disposée sur la couche luminescente (5) et opposée à l'électrode d'affichage (21). L'électrode transparente (2) est séparée en différentes parties fonctionnelles comprenant des électrodes d'affichage (21) formées d'une pluralité de segments pixel de forme spécifique, de bornes (22) menées vers les périphéries du substrat transparent (1) et d'électrodes de câblage (23) permettant la connexion entre les bornes (22) et les électrodes d'affichage (21). L'électrode transparente comprend en outre des bornes (24) pour les électrodes arrière (6).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (I